     1	# GitLab macOS release runbook
     2	
     3	This runbook is the production path for Relux Proxy v0.2.0. It deliberately
     4	fails closed until the Relux-owned GitLab project, accepted commit, protected
     5	runner, and Apple credentials are all present.
     6	
     7	## Current external blocker
     8	
     9	As of 2026-07-28, the production release target is not confirmed:
    10	
    11	| Required identity | Current evidence |
    12	| --- | --- |
    13	| GitLab hostname | Not supplied. `gitlab.com` has no usable local API or SSH authorization. |
    14	| Namespace/project | Not supplied. The only repository remote is `git@github.com:relux-works/relux-proxy.git`. |
    15	| GitLab project ID | Not supplied. |
    16	| Authorized release account | Not supplied. |
    17	| Protected macOS release runner | Not discoverable without the target project. |
    18	| Notarization credentials in GitLab | Not discoverable without the target project. |
    19	
    20	`gitlab.wildberries.ru` is explicitly unrelated and prohibited for every
    21	Relux source push, tag, package, and Release operation. A credential happens to
    22	exist for that host on one development machine; its presence is not
    23	authorization to use it.
    24	
    25	Do not add a GitLab remote, push source, create a tag, or run a release until a
    26	Relux owner replaces the unknown fields above with the exact hostname,
    27	namespace/project, project ID, and authorized account in reviewed project
    28	documentation.
    29	
    30	## One-time project and runner setup
    31	
    32	1. Confirm that the hostname and full namespace/project are owned by Relux.
    33	   Confirm the project ID through the same project page or API and record the
    34	   authorized operator.
    35	2. Enable the project Package Registry and CI/CD.
    36	3. Register a project-locked macOS runner using GitLab's supported user-mode
    37	   `LaunchAgent` and shell executor. Give it both `macos` and `relux-release`
    38	   tags, disable untagged jobs, mark it protected, and do not share it with
    39	   untrusted projects. The runner needs Xcode, Swift, `glab`, `shellcheck`, and
    40	   the standard macOS signing tools.
    41	4. Protect the `v0.2.0` tag so only the release owner can create it.
    42	5. Protect the `production` environment and require the project's chosen
    43	   release approval.
    44	6. Store the following project CI/CD variables. Secret values must be
    45	   **Masked and hidden**, **Protected**, and have variable expansion disabled:
    46	
    47	   | Variable | Handling |
    48	   | --- | --- |
    49	   | `MACOS_CERT_P12_B64` | Base64-encoded Relux Works Developer ID Application certificate plus private key. Secret. |
    50	   | `MACOS_CERT_PASSWORD` | Non-empty password for the PKCS#12 payload. Secret. |
    51	   | `MACOS_KEYCHAIN_PASSWORD` | Temporary CI keychain password. Secret. |
    52	   | `ASC_KEY_ID` | App Store Connect API key ID. Secret metadata. |
    53	   | `ASC_ISSUER_ID` | App Store Connect issuer ID. Secret metadata. |
    54	   | `ASC_KEY_P8_B64` | Base64-encoded App Store Connect API private key. Secret. |
    55	
    56	   Add these non-secret values as Protected variables:
    57	
    58	   | Variable | Required value |
    59	   | --- | --- |
    60	   | `RELUX_GITLAB_HOST` | Exact confirmed hostname, without a scheme. |
    61	   | `RELUX_GITLAB_PROJECT_PATH` | Exact case-sensitive namespace/project path. |
    62	   | `RELUX_ACCEPTED_RELEASE_SHA` | Full lowercase 40-character SHA accepted by review for v0.2.0. |
    63	
    64	GitLab documents that protected variables are limited to protected refs and
    65	that sensitive values should be masked and hidden. Masking is only a log
    66	defense, so the release runner and every pipeline change still require review:
    67	<https://docs.gitlab.com/ci/variables/>.
    68	
    69	GitLab's supported macOS runner setup uses a user-mode `LaunchAgent`; code
    70	signing requires that user session and keychain access:
    71	<https://docs.gitlab.com/runner/install/osx/>.
    72	
    73	## Audited pipeline
    74	
    75	`.gitlab-ci.yml` has three gates:
    76	
    77	1. `validate` runs shell lint, Swift tests, a Swift build, and an ad-hoc-signed
    78	   universal development bundle without production credentials.
    79	2. `release_v0_2_0` runs only for the protected `v0.2.0` tag on the trusted
    80	   `macos` + `relux-release` runner. It compares GitLab's actual host, project
    81	   path, checked-out commit, and runner tags with the protected expected
    82	   values. It imports the certificate into a disposable keychain; builds both
    83	   `arm64` and `x86_64`; signs with the exact Relux Works Developer ID; submits
    84	   the DMG with `notarytool`; requires `Accepted`; saves the notarization log;
    85	   staples and validates the ticket; runs Gatekeeper; and produces checksums.
    86	3. `verify_v0_2_0` downloads all three assets through the GitLab Release's
    87	   direct asset links, verifies that the Release points to the accepted commit,
    88	   compares the published checksum file with the CI-produced file, checks both
    89	   hashes, and proves the stable and versioned DMGs are byte-identical.
    90	
    91	Production jobs are serialized through the
    92	`relux-production-release` resource group. The certificate and API key are
    93	decoded only under a `mktemp` directory; the temporary keychain and decoded
    94	files are removed by an exit trap.
    95	
    96	The package upload uses the automatically scoped `CI_JOB_TOKEN`, following the
    97	GitLab Generic Package Registry contract:
    98	<https://docs.gitlab.com/user/packages/generic_packages/>.
    99	The GitLab Release exposes the package objects as direct asset links:
   100	<https://docs.gitlab.com/api/releases/links/>.
   101	
   102	## Source mirror and tag
   103	
   104	Only after the target table is explicit and authorization has been verified:
   105	
   106	```bash
   107	git remote add relux-gitlab "git@<CONFIRMED_HOST>:<CONFIRMED_NAMESPACE>/relux-proxy.git"
   108	git ls-remote relux-gitlab
   109	git push --dry-run relux-gitlab "<ACCEPTED_SHA>:refs/heads/main"
   110	git push relux-gitlab "<ACCEPTED_SHA>:refs/heads/main"
   111	git tag -s v0.2.0 "<ACCEPTED_SHA>" -m "Relux Proxy v0.2.0"
   112	git push relux-gitlab v0.2.0
   113	```
   114	
   115	Stop if the remote default branch has unrelated history, the dry run names a
   116	different project, the target values disagree, or the protected runner and
   117	variables are absent. Do not force-push around such a mismatch.
   118	
   119	The protected tag pipeline publishes exactly:
   120	
   121	- `ReluxProxy-v0.2.0-universal.dmg`
   122	- `ReluxProxy.dmg`
   123	- `SHA256SUMS`
   124	
   125	The locally configured checkout remains the source of the accepted commit; no
   126	uncommitted working-tree content can enter a tag pipeline.
   127	
   128	## Post-release evidence
   129	
   130	Keep the successful release and verification job artifacts for audit. They
   131	include the source SHA, architectures, signing authority and team ID,
   132	notarization response and log, Gatekeeper result, and published downloads.
   133	
   134	Verify the direct links in the confirmed project:
   135	
   136	```text
   137	https://<CONFIRMED_HOST>/<CONFIRMED_NAMESPACE>/relux-proxy/-/releases/v0.2.0/downloads/ReluxProxy-v0.2.0-universal.dmg
   138	https://<CONFIRMED_HOST>/<CONFIRMED_NAMESPACE>/relux-proxy/-/releases/v0.2.0/downloads/ReluxProxy.dmg
   139	https://<CONFIRMED_HOST>/<CONFIRMED_NAMESPACE>/relux-proxy/-/releases/v0.2.0/downloads/SHA256SUMS
   140	```
   141	
   142	An unsigned, ad-hoc-signed, unstapled, Gatekeeper-rejected, wrong-host, or
   143	wrong-commit artifact is a failed candidate and must never be described as the
   144	production release.
     1	# Relux Proxy v0.2.0
     2	
     3	Relux Proxy v0.2.0 adds saved, independently controlled SSH SOCKS profiles to
     4	the native macOS menu-bar app.
     5	
     6	## Highlights
     7	
     8	- Save multiple profiles with stable identity and a unique local port.
     9	- Connect multiple profiles at once as concurrent local SOCKS endpoints on
    10	  `127.0.0.1`.
    11	- Use an IP address, DNS hostname, or SSH config alias without Relux Proxy
    12	  parsing or rewriting `~/.ssh/config`.
    13	- Leave Account empty to preserve the `User` selected by OpenSSH for a matching
    14	  SSH config alias, or set Account to pass an explicit `-l` user override.
    15	- Start, stop, diagnose, edit, and remove profiles independently. A failed or
    16	  occupied port affects only that profile.
    17	- Migrate the previous single-tunnel preferences once while retaining the old
    18	  keys for rollback compatibility.
    19	
    20	Relux Proxy continues to launch the system `/usr/bin/ssh` client. Each endpoint
    21	is an application SOCKS5 proxy for TCP traffic, not a system VPN. SOCKS-aware
    22	clients should enable SOCKS5h or proxy DNS when the remote SSH host must resolve
    23	private names.
    24	
    25	## Assets
    26	
    27	- `ReluxProxy-v0.2.0-universal.dmg` — versioned Apple silicon and Intel build.
    28	- `ReluxProxy.dmg` — stable-name copy of the same notarized DMG.
    29	- `SHA256SUMS` — SHA-256 hashes for both DMG names.
    30	
    31	The production GitLab pipeline publishes these assets only after verifying the
    32	accepted source commit, Relux GitLab project identity, Developer ID signature,
    33	universal architectures, Apple notarization ticket, stapling, Gatekeeper
    34	assessment, and checksums.
     1	#!/bin/bash
     2	set -euo pipefail
     3	
     4	ROOT="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)"
     5	VERSION="${VERSION:-0.1.0-dev}"
     6	VERSION="${VERSION#v}"
     7	APP="$ROOT/dist/ReluxProxy.app"
     8	DMG="$ROOT/dist/ReluxProxy-v$VERSION-universal.dmg"
     9	STAGE="$ROOT/.build/dmg-root"
    10	
    11	if [[ ! -d "$APP" ]]; then
    12	    echo "error: $APP does not exist; run scripts/build-app.sh first" >&2
    13	    exit 1
    14	fi
    15	
    16	rm -rf "$STAGE" "$DMG"
    17	mkdir -p "$STAGE"
    18	cp -R "$APP" "$STAGE/"
    19	ln -s /Applications "$STAGE/Applications"
    20	hdiutil create -volname "Relux Proxy" -srcfolder "$STAGE" -ov -format UDZO "$DMG"
    21	echo "Built $DMG"
